  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Microsoft 365 SharePoint Online and OneDrive for Business Unified Audit Log → AKSI control ID mapping. SharePoint and OneDrive (collectively the Microsoft 365 file-storage tier) are the dominant Microsoft cloud-content surfaces for enterprises — used pervasively across regulated and unregulated industries for documents, spreadsheets, presentations, and bulk-data exports. Microsoft 365's Unified Audit Log (Purview / Activity API) emits a unified event stream for both products, distinguished by the workload field (OneDrive vs SharePoint). A single importer covers both. Agents accessing, downloading, syncing, and sharing OneDrive/SharePoint content at scale produce the data-loss-prevention signals that govern Microsoft cloud storage: file access, downloads, full-mailbox/full-library sync, anonymous links (the SharePoint exfil parallel to Box public-unprotected), guest sharing, sensitivity-label changes, tenant sharing-policy changes, site-collection admin grants, site permission changes (anonymous access), DLP rule matches, and malware detections. Operation drives the primary control. Application/ServicePrincipal actors downloading sensitive-extension files are top-tier review signals. AnonymousLinkCreated and DLPRuleMatch=high resolve to DE-01 / PR-04 FAIL. Bulk-download and cross-site patterns produce synthetic PR-04 FAIL/FLAG.",
